<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Bonnita lifts interim shr, div.</title>
<headline>Bonnita lifts interim shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to October 31, 1996</p>
<p>		    (millions of rands unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		  14.4    vs  12.5</p>
<p>    Interim div (cts)	 3.5    vs  2.6</p>
<p>    Attrib profit	    31.53   vs  26.65</p>
<p>    Pre- tax		   48.64   vs  39.07</p>
<p>    Interest received	 2.54   vs   0.55 paid</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     15.08   vs  13.72</p>
<p>    Turnover		  501.70   vs 473.21</p>
<p>Div payable: Jan 22</p>
<p>On register: Dec 13</p>
<p>Name - Bonnita Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that increased exports, the weaker rand and value-added products would ensure similar growth in earnings in the second half of the year.</p>
<p>Shareholders will be offered capitalisation shares in lieu of the interim dividend.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
